course: dictionary
lesson: 11360
title: Zoster: a doctors' word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Zoster is a word doctors use, and you will mostly see it inside longer names. Herpes zoster is the medical name for shingles, a painful rash of blisters, usually in a stripe on one side of the body. You do not need to know every word to understand a text, so use the words around zoster to work out what it means.
explain: The sentence says «Chickenpox is caused by the varicella-zoster virus», so zoster is part of the virus's name. The next clues are «spots become blisters and crust over in about a week» and «children stay home until all spots have crusted». Blisters and crusty spots tell you this is an illness, not a place or a person.
explain: Chickenpox is usually mild, but some children get very ill with it. The same virus can sleep in the body for years and wake up later as shingles, which mostly affects older adults. Shingles is the everyday name, and zoster is the doctors' name for it.
fact: Zoster is a medical word, so doctors and scientists use it more than most people do.
fact: «Herpes zoster» is the medical name for shingles.
fact: «Varicella-zoster virus» is the virus that causes chickenpox.
fact: Shingles is a painful rash of blisters, usually in a stripe on one side of the body.
fact: The virus can sleep in the body for years after chickenpox, then wake up later as shingles.
exercise: What is the everyday name for herpes zoster? | *Shingles | Cold sores | Chickenpox | Measles
exercise: Which illness does the varicella-zoster virus cause first? | Shingles | *Chickenpox | Flu | Measles
exercise: The text says spots «crust over in about a week». What does crust over mean? | Grow into wings | Move to another part of the body | *Dry out and form a hard layer | Turn bright blue
test: Shingles is a painful rash of blisters, usually in a stripe on one side of the body. Which medical word means this same illness? | Herpes simplex | *Herpes zoster | Chickenpox | Varicella
test: Shingles mostly affects which people? | *Older adults | Teenagers | Babies | Children at school
exam: Zoster is a doctors' word. Which statement is correct? | Zoster means a stripe of colour | *Zoster is part of the medical name for shingles | Zoster is a flu virus | Zoster is a type of food
